<title>USA: SFX completes Hearst radio acquisitions.</title>
<headline>SFX completes Hearst radio acquisitions.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>SFX Broadcasting Inc said on Tuesday it completed the acquisition of WVTY-FM and WTAE-AM in Pittsburgh and WLTQ-FM and WISN-AM in Milwaukee from Hearst Broadcasting Group for about $35 million.</p>
<p>SFX already has three stations in Pittsburgh -- WDVE-FM, WXDX-FM and WJJJ-FM.</p>
<p>Robert Sillerman, SFX executive chairman, said: &quot;The acquisition of the Pittsburgh stations represents our continuing strategy of filling in-market opportunities.&quot;</p>
<p>The company said it believed it could generate significant revenue and margin enhancements at all of these stations.</p>
<p>((New York newsdesk 212-859-1610))</p>
</text>
